# A MISSING hashed asset ideally 404s so a browser never caches index.html as a
# JS module ("Expected a JavaScript-or-Wasm module script but the server
# responded with a MIME type of text/html"), which used to kill the app behind
# the error boundary for hours.
#
# TWO approaches were tried and BOTH failed on Cloudflare Pages — do not retry
# them without reading this:
#   1. `/assets/*  /assets/:splat  404` — self-referential; measured, it still
#      returned HTTP 200 with index.html. No effect at all.
#   2. `/assets/*  /404.html  404` + a public/404.html — this DID make dead
#      chunks 404, but adding a root 404.html makes Pages serve it as the
#      global not-found page, which OVERRIDES the SPA rule below: every deep
#      link (/charts, /impressum, /portfolio/holdings) broke instantly. Caught
#      in production. Never ship a root 404.html with a client-side router.
#
# So the stale-chunk problem is handled where it can be handled reliably: the
# client. src/components/ErrorBoundary.jsx detects a failed dynamic import and
# reloads once (20s cooldown), which recovers the tab after every deploy.

# SPA fallback for real routes.
